  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ be two positive real numbers. For every integer $n>0$, define $a_n=\\int_\\beta^n\\frac{\\alpha}{u(u^\\alpha+2+u^{-\\alpha})}\\,du$. Then $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}a_n$ is equal to",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{1}{1+\\beta^\\alpha}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{\\beta^\\alpha}{1+\\beta^{-\\alpha}}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{\\beta^\\alpha}{1+\\beta^\\alpha}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{\\beta^{-\\alpha}}{1+\\beta^\\alpha}$"
  },
  "answer": "A",
